"lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"bb73b2f73cbaf609538275ace32f947fb0b6178e11d65f7d65922352c2ce4fbb"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":26325,"output_tokens":2751,"requests":3}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the concrete `bwrap` argv that produces the write-deny (e.g. `--ro-bind / /`, `--bind <scratch> <scratch>`, `--dev /dev`, `--die-with-parent`), symmetric to the spelled-out macOS Seatbelt profile, so the ubuntu-latest CI leg verifies a defined invocation rather than merely `bwrap`-on-PATH.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan states only: '`bwrap` is the committed Linux mechanism' and 'Linux uses `bwrap`, probed at runtime via `shutil.which`' — no argv/flags given.","Contrast: the macOS section gives an explicit profile '(allow default) + (deny file-write*) + an allow-list subpath'.","Evidence class = Unverified: plan admits 'no Linux host was available at planning time, so bwrap's enforcement is an unverified capability until that CI leg is green'.","Capability fact: a bare `bwrap` invocation without --ro-bind/--bind flags does not deny host writes, so 'bwrap present' via shutil.which is not sufficient to deliver the write-deny AC."],"finding":"The Linux bwrap integration names the mechanism and probe (shutil.which) but never specifies the bwrap argv that actually produces the filesystem write-deny, whereas the macOS side spells out a concrete Seatbelt profile. `bwrap` present-on-PATH does not imply the chosen invocation denies writes: a bare `bwrap -- cmd` shares the host filesystem read-write; the deny depends on the specific bind/mount flags (e.g. --ro-bind of the FS root, --bind of the scratch allow-list, --dev, --die-with-parent). Since the plan itself flags bwrap enforcement as its explicitly-UNVERIFIED capability, the flag-level construction is the load-bearing detail and is absent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f15870bff6f648341","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Section 'Linux mechanism: bubblewrap only' and AC line 'Linux uses bwrap, probed at runtime via shutil.which'","norm_id":"nc6c7d4056a42caaa","priority":0.8,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["CI ubuntu-latest leg constructs a bwrap wrapper whose flags omit a read-only root bind, so the three-probe write-deny silently passes host writes through and the enforcement test's DENY probe fails — or worse, an under-constrained bind lets the incident's `rm -rf` shape land on the CI host FS.","A future maintainer reading the plan cannot tell which bwrap flags are load-bearing and reconstructs them from memory, risking a flag-level mismatch analogous to --label vs --labels."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In the 'Linux mechanism' section, add the intended bwrap flag list mirroring the macOS profile: read-only bind the FS root, read-write bind only the allow-list (scratch tree, pytest basetemp, venv, /dev/null), plus --die-with-parent, and state that the shutil.which probe gates that specific invocation.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihoo